/Title (The analysis establishes the presence and extent of duplicate overlap; it does not demonstrate that duplication alone caused every observed performance value. Nevertheless, it provides a strong methodological explanation for the exceptionally optimistic results on the full 1,025-record cohort.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 913 0 R
/Prev 999 0 R
>>
endobj
976 0 obj
<<
/Title (Logistic Regression achieved the highest accuracy \(80.33%\) and an AUC of 0.8712, indicating relative robustness compared with the more complex ensemble models under the reduced sample size.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 914 0 R
/Next 977 0 R
>>
endobj
977 0 obj
<<
/Title (Gaussian Naive Bayes achieved the highest AUC \(0.8842\), indicating strong ranking performance across positive and negative observations despite slightly lower accuracy than Logistic Regression. Tree-based and ensemble models all experienced substantial accuracy reductions after deduplication: Random Forest = 75.41%, XGBoost = 72.13%, Stacking Ensemble = 75.41%. These results indicate that model complexity alone does not guarantee improved performance on a relatively small clinical dataset.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 914 0 R
/Prev 976 0 R
>>
endobj
978 0 obj
<<
/Title (3. Lack of explicit patient identifiers. The duplicate analysis was based on exact feature tuples rather than patient IDs. Identical records cannot automatically be interpreted as belonging to the same patient.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 717 0 R
/Prev 917 0 R
/Next 918 0 R
>>
endobj
